// games/sonic4/test/poison/poison_patchable_partner.emp — POISON (see README).
//
// TARGETS: rule 6 half 2 — the band's ON record must be static too
//          (spec §4.2, Task 8 review; carried into check_band_pairing at parcel P1).
// EXPECTED FRAGMENT: "must be static — a patchable partner"
//
// poison_patchable_band_fire.emp covers rule 6 half 1 (the RESTORE's carrying fire marked
// patchable). This is the other half: the band's ON record marked patchable instead.
//
// A textbook band, ON at line 60 and restore at 140 over $48..$4D, with the ON fire handed
// to `patchable` (channel 0, band 40..100). Every ownership check passes — same id, same
// span, ON above the restore — and check_intervals sees two disjoint fire-line intervals
// (39..99 for the moving record, 139 for the static one), so nothing upstream refuses the
// shape on ordering grounds.
//
// What it spells is a band whose TOP edge moves. Past `lo` (40), Raster_BuildSchedule does
// not emit the record at all (engine/effects/raster.emp, .suppress) — so the restore at
// line 140 still runs and turns the tint off, but the ON op that was supposed to turn it
// on never fired that frame. That is base-over-base, arrived at through a runtime clamp
// instead of an authoring mistake, which is exactly why rule 6 refuses it at BUILD time.
//
// THIS IS THE CHEAPEST THING PARCEL P2b DELETES. The design's §8 argues that a suppressed
// ON is benign (base over base) where a suppressed RESTORE is the measured sweep-5 defect,
// so rule 6 half 2 is precautionary rather than load-bearing once ownership is declared.
// It is kept in force at P1 on purpose: P1 changes no behaviour it does not have to.
//
// PARCEL-P1 NOTE. Built with `band()` and split with an index, for the same reason as
// poison_patchable_band_fire: an unowned hand-authored restore is refused earlier now and
// would never reach this guard.
//
// NO IMPORTS — see poison_four_bands.emp's note.
module games.sonic4.test.poison.poison_patchable_partner

const POISON_PP_BAND = band(60, 140, stream_cram($48, [$0EEE, $0AAA, $0666]), 0)

const POISON_PATCHABLE_PARTNER = patchable([ POISON_PP_BAND[0] ], ch: 0, lo: 40, hi: 100) ++ [ POISON_PP_BAND[1] ]

ensure(raster_program(POISON_PATCHABLE_PARTNER).len > 0,
       "poison_patchable_partner: raster_program returned nothing — this poison no longer reaches the guard it targets")
